ng the enable/disable switch on a node (e.g. Data Visualization, Business Acumen) does not toggle it off: aria-checked stays \\\"true\\\", the node's CSS class/opacity remains unchanged (opacity:1, no disabled/greyed styling), and no visual graying occurs. Repeated clicks (via Playwright click and native DOM click) all left aria-checked=\\\"true\\\". Coverage jumped once from 71% to 73% after the very first click but did not change again on subsequent identical toggle attempts and the node was never visually disabled, indicating the disable feature is non-functional/inconsistent rather than working as specified.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"The details page shows a \\\"Template Library\\\" panel listing pre-built templates (Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) each with job type/department label, competency & connection counts, and topic tags, allowing HR professionals to browse/preview by job type.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Applying a template does not correctly load its structure into the graph editor\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Apply\\\" on the \\\"Software Engineer\\\" template updated the page header (title \\\"Software Engineer\\\", \\\"Engineering\\\", \\\"6 competencies\\\") and the Critical Path stat card (now listing \\\"Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design\\\"), but the actual graph nodes were NOT replaced: the React Flow canvas still contained the previous Data Scientist model's nodes (data-testid rf__node-ml, rf__node-statistics, rf__node-python, rf__node-data-viz, rf__node-business-acumen, rf__node-storytelling) with their old labels \\\"Machine Learning\\\", \\\"Statistical Analysis\\\", etc. This produces an inconsistent state where the header/stats describe one model while the visible graph shows a different, stale one.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Saving a custom template does not prompt for name/description and is not retrievable\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Save Current\\\" immediately shows a toast \\\"Template Saved - Current model configuration has been saved as a template\\\" with no dialog to enter a template name or description. After saving, the Template Library list still shows only the original 5 pre-built templates (Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) - no new custom template entry appears anywhere, and there is no \\\"My Templates\\\" section/tab in the UI at all. Checking localStorage shows it is empty, confirming the saved template is not persisted or retrievable.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Switching between \\\"Recruitment\\\", \\\"Training\\\", and \\\"Promotion\\\" tabs in the Scenario Simulation panel shows distinct simulation content each time: Recruitment shows \\\"Simulate candidate profiles and hiring decisions\\\" with all deltas at 0, Training shows \\\"Model the impact of training programs\\\" with pre-set Level Change +1 for technical/domain, Promotion shows \\\"Assess readiness for role advancement\\\" with Weight Change -5%/+10% presets. Each tab is independently selectable (aria-selected updates) confirming scenario switching works.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On the \\\"Promotion\\\" scenario tab, clicking \\\"Run Simulation\\\" produced a toast \\\"Simulation Applied - Competency levels and weights have been adjusted based on the scenario,\\\" and the Critical Path stat card visibly changed from \\\"3 competencies\\\" (Problem Solving, Programming Languages, System Design) to \\\"4 competencies\\\" (Problem Solving, Programming Languages, Collaboration, +1), demonstrating a quantitative impact of the scenario adjustment on a key indicator without manual refresh.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No state persistence and no explicit save/load mechanism\", \"actual\": \"After making edits to the Data Scientist model (moved the \\\"Machine Learning\\\" node from its default position, changed its Level from Advanced back down triggering Coverage 73%->67% and a Risk Gap alert, then separately applied \\\"Software Engineer\\\" template and ran a Promotion simulation), reloading the page (full navigation to http://localhost:7097/) returned to the Models list, and re-opening the \\\"Data Scientist\\\" model showed it fully reset to its original state: Coverage back to 71% (not 67%), Critical Path back to \\\"3 competencies\\\" (Machine Learning, Python Programming, Statistical Analysis) instead of the simulated 4, the Scenario Simulation tab reset to \\\"Recruitment\\\" (not the \\\"Promotion\\\" tab last used), and the Machine Learning node's transform back to translate(0px, 0px) i.e. its original position (the drag was not preserved). The \\\"Save\\\" button in the header shows only a generic label with no confirmation of what it saves or where, and clicking through the flow earlier (\\\"Save Current\\\" in Template Library, tested under FT-8) does not persist to localStorage or any retrievable store. There is no explicit save/load/session-restore mechanism, and all in-progress edits are lost on navigation away and back.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Cannot verify prevention of invalid edges to disabled nodes - edge creation mechanism itself is non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Attempted to create new dependency edges by dragging from a node's source connection handle to another node's target handle (React Flow connectable handles present in DOM, class react-flow__handle source/target). Tried business-acumen(source) -> data-viz(target), a pair with no existing edge, and data-viz(source) -> storytelling(target). In both cases, the edge list (queried via .react-flow__edge aria-label) remained unchanged (still exactly the original 5 pre-defined edges) - no new edge was created. No \\\"Add Edge/Connection\\\" button or context menu exists anywhere in the UI either. Combined with FT-5's finding that the node enable/disable switch does not functionally toggle a node's disabled state, there is no way to construct or observe the specific invalid scenario (adding an edge to a disabled node) because neither disabling a node nor creating a new edge works at all in this build. The constraint cannot be confirmed as implemented/enforced.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changing the \\\"Machine Learning\\\" node's level via its segmented level selector immediately updated the Coverage stat card from 73% to 67% and Avg Level from 3.6 to 3.3, without any manual refresh, confirming real-time recalculation on structural change.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Editing operations are purely client-side (browser_network_requests shows zero non-static/API requests triggered by node/edge interactions) so there is no network round-trip latency. Measured via MutationObserver timing that clicking a competency's level-segment button produced a DOM mutation (stat/level update) in ~81ms, well within perceptible-lag thresholds. Earlier FT-3 node drag rendered smoothly in real time with the connected edge path updating continuously to follow the node, and IX-13's coverage/avg-level recalculation and the Promotion scenario simulation (FT-10) both completed and reflected in the UI immediately with no loading spinners, skeleton states, or visible delay, confirming responsive graph editing at the current (moderate, 6-node) model complexity.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Details page renders a React Flow directed graph: nodes labeled with competency names (Machine Learning, Statistical Analysis, Python Programming, Data Visualization, Business Acumen, Data Storytelling) each showing level/weight/category, and edges labeled \\\"Edge from X to Y\\\" with percentage weight badges (e.g. \\\"Edge from python to ml\\\" 90%), plus zoom/pan/minimap controls confirming interactivity.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Critical Path card shows \\\"3 competencies\\\": Machine Learning, Python Programming, Statistical Analysis - will verify it updates after structural change in later item.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After lowering the level of the critical \\\"Machine Learning\\\" competency, Risk Gaps stat updated in real time from \\\"0 identified\\\" to \\\"1 identified\\\" and listed \\\"Machine Learning\\\" as the risk gap, confirming real-time risk gap analysis after structural change (re-confirms earlier CT-17 pass with concrete before/after evidence).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Lowering Machine Learning's level to the lowest segment triggered a prominent alert box (role=alert) titled \\\"Competency Gap Alert\\\" with text \\\"1 competency below recommended level: Machine Learning. Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\", displayed directly below the stats cards in a highly visible position.\"}]}"
